soccer in 40 degrees celsius heat  the players wear dortmund and bayern  munich shirts but this match is far  away from the bundesliga in kunduz  province in northern afghanistan  sophiola zahiwal has a dream to play in  afghanistan's premier league and one day  perhaps in spain or germany  he also dreams of peace  if there's conflict it's impossible to  play football  because people flee the country  playing soccer in afghanistan isn't  without risk  there's the constant threat of a  terrorist attack kunduz province remains  dangerous  even more now that german troops are  withdrawing  the taliban controls some areas  soccer is huge in afghanistan and so are  its superstars such as cristiano ronaldo  who's supposedly more popular than  president karzai  sofia watches the champions league with  his friends  real madrid are playing galatasaray  is his favorite player today he's  wearing a manchester city jersey  and socks and shorts from his favorite  spanish teams  the 24 year old is serious about his  soccer career  but he's worried about the future of  afghanistan  i've been playing since i was a boy i  love the game with  all my heart but if the taliban came  back  that would affect soccer too sofia  and his friends were among the hundreds  of thousands who filled the streets when  afghanistan won the south asian  championship in september  they beat india 2-0 a victory that  seemed to give the entire nation a much  needed boost  and this is the victory song a catchy  tune that celebrates the historic win  and pays tribute to the players who  brought the trophy home  soccer in afghanistan suffered under the  taliban  but the game has come on considerably in  recent times  the country now has its own premier  league  shafiq gauhari ran several german-funded  infrastructure development projects in  afghanistan before turning his hand to  soccer  soccer can help people come together and  become friends with one another  when that happens i think it can make an  important contribution  to peace  an important contribution perhaps but  soccer alone cannot deliver  lasting peace to afghanistan
 

